    {
      "sample_index": 4,
      "text": "To find the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Understand the properties of a triangle's angles:**\n   The sum of the interior angles of any triangle is always \\(180^\\circ\\).\n\n2. **Define the mean value:**\n   The mean value of a set of numbers is calculated by summing all the values and then dividing by the number of values.\n\n3. **Sum the interior angles:**\n   Since the sum of the interior angles of any triangle is \\(180^\\circ\\), we can denote this sum as:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Sum of angles} = 180^\\circ\n   \\]\n\n4. **Count the number of angles:**\n   A triangle has three interior angles.\n\n5. **Calculate the mean value:**\n   The mean value is given by dividing the sum of the angles by the number of angles:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Mean value} = \\frac{\\text{Sum of angles}}{\\text{Number of angles}} = \\frac{180^\\circ}{3}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the mean value of the measures of the three interior angles of any triangle is \\(\\boxed{60^\\circ}\\).",
